/Title (The Ministry of Civil Resilience has confirmed that permanent settlements across multiple regions have been declared uninhabitable following continued soil toxicity, collapsing infrastructure and unpredictable environmental conditions. Entire cities now lie abandoned beneath layers of industrial ash, while toxic dust storms regularly force surviving communities to relocate. Traditional housing has become increasingly obsolete as stable ground becomes scarce and access to clean water continues to decline.Across continents, abandoned skylines stand as silent reminders of an industrial civilization that exhausted the ecosystems upon which it depended.)
